#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105679 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a4270f2-daf1-532d-804a-f293b6f1a8be" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Polygon"}] :question/id #uuid "36445a36-7b68-5ba1-847e-7fd720138dd6" :question/math-academy-id "e-7859" :question/problem "The stretch $S(x,y) = \\left(\\dfrac{3}{2}x,2y\\right)$ is applied to the polygon shown below. Find the resulting polygon.\n\n![](images/a3/a36f0ee4e491e0518041f7e033392b9f16e12c4e2501e707d8328af78aa89efd.png)" :question/worked-solution "To stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(2,1)$, $(4,1)$, $(2,2)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2,1) & ↦(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2,\\,2\\cdot 1)=(3,2) \\\\ (4,1) & ↦(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 4,\\,2\\cdot 1)=(6,2) \\\\ (2,2) & ↦(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2,\\,2\\cdot 2)=(3,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/b9/b961a446536bddbe6ff529e7ca2973c8e957c185ef4d6f00b9255d09baa9d3cc.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105680 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "043fb5ef-143e-53cc-b83a-15df50446af4" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Combined Stretches Using Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "228d023c-b74d-56a9-ab02-638594472f43" :question/math-academy-id "e-7860" :question/problem "What function represents the combined stretch of factor $4$ in the $x$-direction and factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ in the $y$-direction?" :question/worked-solution "- A stretch in the $x$-direction of factor $4$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto (4x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch in the $y$-direction of factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ can be represented by the function \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(4x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105681 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28d37803-32d2-5b80-aa78-2f0d728e18fe" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "50e74298-c5c0-5bda-bb64-18778f156508" :question/math-academy-id "e-7861" :question/problem "The point $(2,5)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-2.$ What is the resulting point?" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(2x,y\\right).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $-2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left(x,-2y\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto \\left({\\color{blue}2}x,{\\color{red}-2}y\\right).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(2,5) \\mapsto \\left(2\\cdot 2, \\, -2\\cdot5 \\right) = (4,-10).\n$$\n\n![](images/0d/0d050ec1579f2ea2b37c01f2d7b60fd6580b6bc4766fcdd66005e1c2c103b8c7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a4270f2-daf1-532d-804a-f293b6f1a8be" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Polygon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a238a9-2b8f-567b-ad80-f0ef6c09bdac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3c/3c0fa57f821f0970652cc9c7cfd29c0bf84c86d9cf312092a4ae620cf23f9c0c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534369} {:answer/id #uuid "aec615b7-c75a-5947-b8d9-82deedc574e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/41/41d19c613c87d03a27d223b273de252d204ef4bdae9bbef9ccdb7a6b9a052799.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534656} {:answer/id #uuid "d6050368-ce12-5a9c-8193-7fed60bb845a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/9026ba33e157b287501339fb6978b2ccb6704af2e973211f9212c6f800fc6f23.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534747} {:answer/id #uuid "db730826-ef16-5c39-810b-7a3e33ae4b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/340fd3449d3c0ca638fd0ed214e88fce3dfb70f5625e7944b64136a6c240bc65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534758} {:answer/id #uuid "ffdb2a34-d0f3-5827-8225-39b57eb2abab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f1/f101601f17806447c06e1c876f3beb92d5fa97bf9019cbea86f0496f56b1fb37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffdb2a34-d0f3-5827-8225-39b57eb2abab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f1/f101601f17806447c06e1c876f3beb92d5fa97bf9019cbea86f0496f56b1fb37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534827} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8174907-9a6c-5434-be88-361402b60a64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c9a7b3c-46d7-5715-a15a-49321cace888" :question/math-academy-id "q-45448" :question/problem "![](images/9f/9fd4e55e5de09555b5a1fe05f8fb5f47b03d3b0cd9d96cbdca526f0d357d0afb.png)\n\nA stretch of factor $3$ in the $x$-direction and $2$ in the $y$-direction is applied to the polygon shown above. Which of the following is the resulting polygon?" :question/worked-solution "A stretch of factor $3$ in the $x$-direction and $2$ in the $y$-direction can be represented by the following function:\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,2y)\n$$\n\nTo stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(1,3)$, $(1,-2)$, $(-2,2)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1,3) & ↦(3\\cdot 1,2\\cdot 3)=(3,6) \\\\ (1,-2) & ↦(3\\cdot 1,2\\cdot (-2))=(3,-4) \\\\ (-2,2) & ↦(3\\cdot (-2),2\\cdot 2)=(-6,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/6c/6c77ca7fa6efa27125c131c629b5afeba784b8ca4fd1039530879c2ec177b8dc.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a4270f2-daf1-532d-804a-f293b6f1a8be" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Polygon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b01cf01-6055-5206-8628-9df03691af89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/36e66a86bca25711839b36dd2597d8b8b96c5a9c531c6fa77ee8a13dec831d41.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534286} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5b02cb-0bdf-5f7c-b77e-43fafe31913a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b4e9383b4264089dc6880e28c16e29b358134e67b6265fc0dfeb76559e6abb9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534486} {:answer/id #uuid "be4c840b-bbd5-502e-bbc6-846b75b62a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e70b2a1569a5b46118ce4ae169a163c02ed4e34fdba27f4c2f16f0e7e1c0896e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534690} {:answer/id #uuid "c118275d-2f2f-56fb-b192-cf9482e8d88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/88/88d18cd1bdbcf7cbe3eb50864607632380a3a1bb8f3271e17f857303742e9615.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534695} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0bc394-3fcc-570c-803b-19a1df9fee48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bdc4d5b733df0f7293224cf26f9eacc675c248004ceeb74717bdcb3cc88f8010.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b01cf01-6055-5206-8628-9df03691af89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/36e66a86bca25711839b36dd2597d8b8b96c5a9c531c6fa77ee8a13dec831d41.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534286} :answer-field/id #uuid "20836d9f-5b2c-5007-984d-6198830d570b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63c2d1f3-bff7-58f3-9c73-044cb81121d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-45450" :question/problem "![](images/76/7625ed8002bbd684ba004185f357e8b8e9b3384857684ef836ccd4a019a317cd.png)\n\nThe stretch $S(x,y)=(\\frac{1}{2}x,\\frac{1}{3}y)$ is applied to the polygon shown above. Which of the following is the resulting polygon?" :question/worked-solution "To stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(4,6)$, $(5,-3)$, $(-6,-6)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4,6) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6)=(2,2) \\\\ (6,-3) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-3))=(3,-1) \\\\ (-6,-6) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6),\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-6))=(-3,-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](images/aa/aa9f0b7c785c5c830c0e902f500fe0998df4c4ee8ace07af6989cf9aad2a88ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "043fb5ef-143e-53cc-b83a-15df50446af4" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Combined Stretches Using Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "127c4155-1f19-5cc4-9c19-a0d3041bb683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(x,4y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534304} {:answer/id #uuid "1f295345-6a68-5dab-b6a6-eb286ab41b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(4x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534326} {:answer/id #uuid "29faaffe-98fa-5db1-917a-0be3d37da2a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(3x,4y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534352} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f2a443-9d68-52a6-97a1-f6b7ae598ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(3x,y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534701} {:answer/id #uuid "c4841df8-55cd-574b-95b3-f90d508b11f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(4x,3y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29faaffe-98fa-5db1-917a-0be3d37da2a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(3x,4y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534352} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff7570d2-23c8-593e-ae05-f7eefecf996a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "501956c6-823d-5f9c-8694-d92497158079" :question/math-academy-id "q-88610" :question/problem "What function represents a stretch of factor $4$ and invariant $x$-axis, followed by a stretch of factor $3$ and invariant $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "- A stretch of factor $4$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,4y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $3$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,4y).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28d37803-32d2-5b80-aa78-2f0d728e18fe" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae5059f-bcf0-56ad-8d2b-a7753f3f2165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105353} {:answer/id #uuid "d7670310-6908-57ff-a1cc-003fdf97fe7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105355} {:answer/id #uuid "23bd6a64-92c7-5a5d-a870-0e7c3474eddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534342} {:answer/id #uuid "4f90ff09-0b90-5a43-aeef-b149ae5cc47f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534421} {:answer/id #uuid "aac6e0c5-e450-5a3c-b210-84f3ab8b09c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ae5059f-bcf0-56ad-8d2b-a7753f3f2165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105353} :answer-field/id #uuid "af8b2139-6d53-5b18-926c-04ee1c2734e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20947e98-c606-5c7e-861f-e50700e68b13" :question/math-academy-id "q-88617" :question/problem "The point $(4,2)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $-3.$ What is the resulting point?" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $-3$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,-3y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,-3y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(4,2)↦(2\\cdot 4,\\,-3\\cdot 2)=(8,-6).\n$$\n\n![](images/ab/ab3fda7652a99346f6d33e11b43d3401e2a427ab6d2f54c0f8717733fb3f892c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535074 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "043fb5ef-143e-53cc-b83a-15df50446af4" :knowledge-point/title "Representing Combined Stretches Using Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2598ef-553f-5520-951f-18966c644f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(x,5y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534357} {:answer/id #uuid "3497c86f-9024-5137-b2c8-e6adf9725485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(5x,2y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534364} {:answer/id #uuid "4982073b-5efe-5343-96ae-651ab5588fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(x+2,y+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534406} {:answer/id #uuid "84e5e9a1-8e72-51e7-beea-35ed9007c1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(2x,5y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534552} {:answer/id #uuid "8c35c4d1-88a9-5e67-8726-07d37cd1ee31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(x+5,y+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84e5e9a1-8e72-51e7-beea-35ed9007c1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x,y)↦(2x,5y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534552} :answer-field/id #uuid "1736b26d-c788-5e6f-a118-e706913fe93b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd1b71b5-3284-5639-806c-2226f712ef21" :question/math-academy-id "q-88759" :question/problem "What function represents a stretch of factor $5$ and invariant $x$-axis, followed by a stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "- A stretch of factor $5$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,5y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,5y).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28d37803-32d2-5b80-aa78-2f0d728e18fe" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Combined Stretch to a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3659512c-606b-5c80-b2da-172375a8b128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,20)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534368} {:answer/id #uuid "557eab86-52f5-5159-b8ac-f4a8b98acf3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-10,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534437} {:answer/id #uuid "658c09db-7834-5584-8ce0-05b1a462f6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(20,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534469} {:answer/id #uuid "acda96ba-19db-5933-a31e-fe52d93e2788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534653} {:answer/id #uuid "c8928c1b-b157-5390-b635-b1b7ade3cde5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8928c1b-b157-5390-b635-b1b7ade3cde5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534718} :answer-field/id #uuid "9119a8a3-997b-5c35-bcb5-0ad9de0ba66d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "758a989a-3043-5362-867a-7a0673f17cc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-88767" :question/problem "The point $(5,-5)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $2.$ What is the resulting point?" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,2y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,2y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(5,-5)↦(2\\cdot 5,\\,2\\cdot (-5))=(10,-10).\n$$\n\n![](images/8e/8e3eccf9b9190db3c19e2d49d633763d420947daa12929a8516fcf066465165d.png)"}]}
